{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"Styling","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The built-in style variants, alternative Loading placeholders, and the theming configuration point — everything beyond the out-of-the-box defaults for tuning how a placeholder looks without writing a fully custom one."}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every default placeholder ships two independent levers: a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"style"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (how big a footprint it expects to own) and, in SwiftUI, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"theme","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (what color\/font it uses). On top of the default spinner, two alternative Loading placeholders cover the other common shapes a loading state takes: a pulsing skeleton, and a redacted mirror of the real content."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"compact-style","text":"`.compact` style"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStatePlaceholderStyle","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" controls how much space a default placeholder expects to fill. Every default placeholder’s initializer takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"style:"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter, defaulting to "},{"code":".standard","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the full-screen treatment: a full-size icon, and, for the Loading spinner, filling all available space."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass "},{"code":".compact","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to embed the same placeholder in a card or section instead of a whole screen: a smaller icon, smaller text, and — for the Loading spinner — no more forcing itself to fill the available space:"}]},{"code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(style: .compact)","ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView(style: .compact)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".compact"},{"type":"text","text":" always keeps a vertical icon-above-text layout, regardless of the device’s orientation — a card’s size is dictated by the card, not the device, unlike the automatic landscape-iPhone icon-beside-text switch "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".standard"},{"type":"text","text":" makes on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Alternative Loading placeholders","anchor":"Alternative-Loading-placeholders","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — the spinner — are what every default-wired "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateContainerView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateViewController"},{"type":"text","text":" shows. Two opt-in alternatives cover the other common shapes a loading state takes:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateShimmerLoadingView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateShimmerLoadingUIView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": a pulsing skeleton of a circular avatar plus two text-line placeholders, for a generic “something’s coming” look that doesn’t need to know the real content’s shape."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateRedactedLoadingView"},{"type":"text","text":": renders your real content view through SwiftUI’s "},{"code":".redacted(reason: .placeholder)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the placeholder mirrors the exact shape of the content it’s standing in for. SwiftUI-only — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"redacted(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" has no UIKit equivalent."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"code":["ScreenStateShimmerLoadingView()","","ScreenStateRedactedLoadingView {","    ArticleRow(article: .placeholder)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both respect Reduce Motion and Increase Contrast the same way the default spinner does; see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Theming","anchor":"Theming","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStatesTheme","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lets a SwiftUI app theme every default placeholder at once — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tint"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"titleFont"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageFont"},{"type":"text","text":" — instead of passing a fully custom placeholder view at every call site. Set it once via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.screenStatesTheme(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" on a container view, and every default placeholder beneath it in the view hierarchy (including "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screens